<title>UK: Perry to become Centrica chairman - Brit Gas.</title>
<headline>Perry to become Centrica chairman - Brit Gas.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Gas on Friday confirmed that Sir Michael Perry, the former Unilever Plc chairman, will become Centrica's non-executive chairman from July 1, succeeding Richard Giordano.</p>
<p>Giordano is currently chairman of British Gas. He will remain chairman of BG Plc, the renamed rump of British Gas after the demerger.</p>
<p>Centrica will be formed through a demerger in February and will mainly consist of British Gas' supply business.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
